&lt;h3&gt;


  Frequently Asked Questions
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What did Claude design in Anthropic’s scorpion-toxin study?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Claude generated &lt;em&gt;de novo&lt;/em&gt; minibinder candidates intended to bind five scorpion neurotoxins associated with four scorpion species or regions. Anthropic reported 318,484 designs and 553,052 design-toxin pairs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Did Anthropic create an antivenom?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. Anthropic says it has not validated toxin neutralization in cells or living systems and does not claim to have produced an antivenom.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How were the selected designs tested?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Anthropic sent 211 designs to Adaptyv Bio and Twist Bioscience. Adaptyv Bio used a cell-free expression system, while Twist Bioscience used mammalian-cell expression of Fc fusions and surface plasmon resonance to assess binding.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What was the laboratory result?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seventeen of the 211 designs selected for testing met Anthropic’s predefined criteria for binding to the toxins. This result concerns binding, not efficacy, safety, or neutralization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Can research teams broadly access these Claude protein-design capabilities?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Anthropic says the capabilities described in the study are not broadly available. The campaign is an exploratory research demonstration rather than a general product availability announcement.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h3&gt;


  Conclusion
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s scorpion-toxin campaign offers laboratory-tested evidence that Claude can assist an early protein-design workflow, from generating candidates to prioritizing designs for experimental follow-up. The 17 binding hits are an encouraging research result, but they are not evidence of an antivenom or a replacement for cellular, animal, and other downstream validation. Its clearest significance is as a measured example of how AI may expand scientific hypothesis generation while keeping experimental evidence at the center of the process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ending the foundations stage, and keep moving forward!&lt;/p&gt;

